GENERATE_PLOT_POINT_PROMPT = '\nCreate a preliminary plot plan spanning all {{EpisodeNums}} episodes of a serialized story. This plan will serve as a reference for a four-phase script outline; it is not screenplay prose.\n\nGenre: {{Topic}}\nWorld: {{WorldView}}\nCore premise: {{StoryOutline}}\nPrincipal characters: {{RoleInfo}}\n{% if Reference and Reference.strip() %}Creative reference: {{Reference}}\n{% endif %}\nRequirements:\n1. Build the main plot around the protagonist\'s desire, obstacles, choices, and consequences. Events must be causally clear, while character states and relationships accumulate change over time.\n2. Allocate appropriate room for setup, development, escalation, and resolution. Subplots may serve the main plot and character arcs, but avoid repeating the same conflict or advancing through unmotivated twists. Establish the protagonist’s urgent goal and central conflict early, then develop a compact serial narrative through escalating obstacles, consequential revelations, and shifts in the situation.\n3. Each beat covers a continuous episode range. Ranges must not overlap, leave gaps, or exceed the episode count. Major sequences can span multiple episodes; transitions need only the space they require.\n4. Plan major reveals, relationship turns, transfers of important objects, and phase outcomes clearly enough to support later continuity checks.\n\nOutput only a valid JSON object, with no extra fields:\n{\n  "plot_planning": [\n    {\n      "plot_id": 1,\n      "title": "Beat title",\n      "episode_range": [1, 3],\n      "plot_desc": [{"episode_id": 1, "plot_desc": "Core action, obstacle, and outcome; at most 60 English words"}]\n    }\n  ],\n  "plot_stuck_point_id": 1,\n  "stuck_point_desc": "Why the setup, major turns, and ending are placed as planned"\n}\n'
GENERATE_OUTLINE_BY_SCRIPT_PROMPT = '\nWrite a four-phase script outline for the complete series based on the core premise, world, and characters, using the preliminary plot plan as a reference.\n\nGenre: {{Topic}}\nWorld: {{WorldView}}\nCore premise: {{StoryOutline}}\nCharacters: {{RoleInfo}}\n{% if Reference and Reference.strip() %}Creative reference: {{Reference}}\n{% endif %}Preliminary plot plan (for reference): {{ScriptProposal}}\n\nRequirements:\n1. Preserve the core premise, main characters, and world rules. Organize events into Setup, Development, Climax, and Resolution.\n2. For each event, make clear what triggers it, the participants\' goals and actions, the obstacles, the outcome, and what changes in characters, relationships, knowledge, objects, or environment.\n3. Adjacent events must connect naturally. Significant discoveries, shifts in allegiance, transfers of objects, changes of time or place, and changes in ability require a plausible process.\n4. You may add subplots that enrich character arcs and causal transitions. Use the preliminary plot plan as a reference, enriching its plot, dramatic conflicts, and related elements, and adjusting its event sequence, pacing, and planned outcomes as needed while remaining consistent with the core premise.\n5. Avoid padding with repetitive conflict or sacrificing established motivation and facts for a twist.\n\nOutput only a valid JSON object, with no extra fields:\n{\n  "title": "Series title",\n  "background": "Established pre-story facts, initial circumstances, and central conflict",\n  "framework": [\n    {"stage": "Setup", "event_list": [{"event": "Specific event and its causal outcome"}]},\n    {"stage": "Development", "event_list": [{"event": "Specific event and its causal outcome"}]},\n    {"stage": "Climax", "event_list": [{"event": "Specific event and its causal outcome"}]},\n    {"stage": "Resolution", "event_list": [{"event": "Specific event and its causal outcome"}]}\n  ],\n  "highlights": "Distinctive elements that arise organically from character and causality",\n  "summary": "The complete story, relationship changes, and theme in causal order"\n}\n'
